elp  separate you from most of the people who  are out there okay number two pass the  tests okay with oDesk you give  a chance to look for to apply for  different tasks so it could be English  speaking tasks it could be customer  service tests it could be data entry  tests it could be about programming a  specific language it tests you and as an  employer they'll often look at that if  I'm hiring a PHP programmer I want to  know that you passed and scored well on  the PHP programming test okay it's not  enough just to pass it you got to score  while I don't want somebody who can just  barely get by and so when you're taking  the test prepare for it study for it  don't don't have something else going on  in the background listening to youtube  videos or being distracted on chat take  it seriously because employers will take  those test scores seriously so take the  test and prepare for them number three  pay attention to the job application  whenever I put out a job I get hundreds  of people who are interested in it which  is great but most people never fully  read the job application now I make it a  little difficult on purpose because as  an employer I got killed trying to go  through all these applications so I'll  write one big ugly paragraph and in the  middle write something like how many  Twitter followers do I have and put that  in the first sentence of your job  application and 80% of people don't do  that 80% of people won't even read that  line and give me my answer so you think  I'm going to hire that person no read  the job application okay this may sound  like simple basic things that most  people are not doing it okay number four  find a way to make it personal find a  way to stand out okay the ones who I've  hired who made it an impression on me  are the ones who always left something  personal in the job application like I  went to your website and I really  enjoyed whatever article or I saw your  YouTube video and it really spoke to me  you don't wanna you don't wanna lie  about something you want to be honest  you want to make it personal but that  extra little touch immediately makes you  stand out over everybody else so do it  and in the last one my last point number  five is over-deliver okay because the  most popular people I find on oDesk they  already have jobs with somebody else  because those employers don't want to  let them go over deliver be responsive  the thing I hate the most and the thing  that worries people a lot is  communication if somebody writes to you  especially from different time zones you  want to make sure that you're responding  quickly and you're giving your employee  back to your employer more than what  they asked for  make them love to have you write they're  hiring you for their business you need  to become an important part of their  business you have to be so important  that if you leave there they're in a big  hole that's how not only you get hired  but how you can start increasing your  prices you have to be super important to  that business okay so those are my how  many five tips one have a picture to  answer the questions on the test and  prepare for it three read the Job  Description everything through four  personalize it and number five over  deliver like crazy for your employer  that's it you do that you'll be an O  test superstar believe those are  watching like a video give it a thumbs  up below if you have a question for me  or comment leave it below  I love seen those come in to thank you  so much and I'll see you soon
 

